1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,571
You've been writing leads,

2
00:00:02,021 --> 00:00:03,671
and a lead happens once.

3
00:00:04,571 --> 00:00:06,959
Today you write the other kind of quest,

4
00:00:07,409 --> 00:00:10,608
the kind a crew can take again and again.

5
00:00:12,408 --> 00:00:16,516
That's what a job is: a station offers it, the crew takes it,

6
00:00:16,966 --> 00:00:18,631
they do it, and they're paid.

7
00:00:19,531 --> 00:00:21,837
And when they come back, it's there again.

8
00:00:23,037 --> 00:00:26,387
Here's the whole life of a job, in five stages.

9
00:00:27,287 --> 00:00:33,170
First it's offered, when Comms selects a station, and each job is a button, with its pay.

10
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:39,786
Then it's taken, and it goes into the Quest Log, under the ship's name.

11
00:00:40,686 --> 00:00:43,558
Then it's done, when its ending comes true,

12
00:00:44,008 --> 00:00:46,008
wherever the ship happens to be.

13
00:00:47,808 --> 00:00:52,126
Then it's paid, in credits, and in standing with the side that offered it.

14
00:00:53,026 --> 00:00:54,299
And then it's offered again.

15
00:00:56,099 --> 00:00:59,115
Now, the template gave you three jobs,

16
00:00:59,565 --> 00:01:01,455
and two of them have no ending at all.

17
00:01:02,356 --> 00:01:04,910
A crew can take them, and never finish them.

18
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:08,726
An ending is one line, Done when,

19
00:01:09,176 --> 00:01:12,394
and it's an order to the captain in plain words.

20
00:01:14,194 --> 00:01:15,607
There are five first words.

21
00:01:16,507 --> 00:01:20,783
Destroy. Recover. Scan. Reach. And dock.

22
00:01:21,683 --> 00:01:24,476
After the word comes a number, and what to count.

23
00:01:26,276 --> 00:01:29,837
So, for Patrol: Done when, destroy three enemies.

24
00:01:30,737 --> 00:01:32,818
Enemies is a word the game knows.

25
00:01:33,268 --> 00:01:35,990
It means anything at war with the crew.

26
00:01:37,790 --> 00:01:39,526
The crew never sees that line.

27
00:01:39,976 --> 00:01:41,422
They read the description under it,

28
00:01:41,872 --> 00:01:43,969
so the order goes there too.

29
00:01:45,169 --> 00:01:47,256
Salvage is the Gleaners' job.

30
00:01:48,156 --> 00:01:51,461
Its ending is, recover two tech,

31
00:01:51,911 --> 00:01:55,062
and tech is a key from your Goods chapter.

32
00:01:56,862 --> 00:01:58,046
Now look at the reward.

33
00:01:58,946 --> 00:02:01,699
After the credits I'm adding a comma,

34
00:02:02,149 --> 00:02:06,185
and then a deed, the same three words as in Lecture Four.

35
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,641
A side, a trait, and a number.

36
00:02:11,441 --> 00:02:14,831
So this job pays, and it pleases the Gleaners.

37
00:02:15,731 --> 00:02:18,496
But the farmers hear who's been stripping wrecks,

38
00:02:18,946 --> 00:02:21,532
and they think a little less of the crew.

39
00:02:23,332 --> 00:02:24,792
And mind that comma.

40
00:02:25,242 --> 00:02:27,075
Leave it out, and the credits are paid,

41
00:02:27,525 --> 00:02:30,482
the deed is dropped, and lint gives you a warning about it.

42
00:02:31,682 --> 00:02:33,686
Three more jobs, quickly.

43
00:02:34,586 --> 00:02:38,071
A survey, which ends when Science scans a dead ship.

44
00:02:39,871 --> 00:02:41,977
A run home, against the clock.

45
00:02:42,877 --> 00:02:44,855
Fails when, ten minutes,

46
00:02:45,305 --> 00:02:47,672
and a penalty if it does.

47
00:02:48,572 --> 00:02:50,780
You know both of those lines from Class One.

48
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,864
And a strike, at tier three.

49
00:02:55,764 --> 00:02:59,897
That one's only offered to a crew the Compact really trusts.

50
00:03:01,697 --> 00:03:03,874
The relay run does something else for me.

51
00:03:04,774 --> 00:03:05,860
It ends at home,

52
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:08,412
so it's a way back that pays.

53
00:03:09,612 --> 00:03:11,212
Now look at what's under the fence.

54
00:03:12,112 --> 00:03:15,349
That's the job's briefing, and it's a page, not a line.

55
00:03:17,149 --> 00:03:18,762
Before the crew takes a job,

56
00:03:19,212 --> 00:03:22,521
all they see is a button, with a name and a price.

57
00:03:23,421 --> 00:03:26,625
Once they've taken it, the Quest Log shows them all of this.

58
00:03:28,425 --> 00:03:32,957
The first line puts the Assay Office beside the words, in three dimensions.

59
00:03:33,857 --> 00:03:36,344
It's the same model as the station's Art line,

60
00:03:36,794 --> 00:03:38,141
so they see who's paying.

61
00:03:39,941 --> 00:03:42,713
An empty line starts a new paragraph.

62
00:03:43,613 --> 00:03:45,426
The first one is the order,

63
00:03:45,876 --> 00:03:47,883
and the second is why it matters.

64
00:03:49,683 --> 00:03:52,366
And an icon can start a line, or be a bullet.

65
00:03:53,266 --> 00:03:54,918
An hourglass for the clock,

66
00:03:55,368 --> 00:03:57,819
and a crosshair for the hulls.

67
00:03:58,719 --> 00:04:00,730
Lint checks the icon names,

68
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:02,428
and the model's name too,

69
00:04:02,878 --> 00:04:05,083
so a misspelled one gets a warning.

70
00:04:06,283 --> 00:04:08,630
A job nobody offers is never seen.

71
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:11,368
So, back up to the sides.

72
00:04:13,168 --> 00:04:15,920
The farmers get patrol, escort and strike.

73
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:19,384
The miners get the survey and the relay run.

74
00:04:21,184 --> 00:04:23,286
I'm taking the escort away from the miners,

75
00:04:23,736 --> 00:04:26,696
because it ends at their own front door.

76
00:04:27,596 --> 00:04:29,291
A job that ends at a place

77
00:04:29,741 --> 00:04:32,953
belongs to a side that lives somewhere else.

78
00:04:34,153 --> 00:04:36,317
I save, and lint says clean.

79
00:04:38,117 --> 00:04:41,007
And today that's less than half the check.

80
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,989
Lint knows the five first words,

81
00:04:44,439 --> 00:04:46,643
so a misspelled one gets a warning.

82
00:04:47,543 --> 00:04:49,516
But it doesn't read what comes after.

83
00:04:51,316 --> 00:04:52,849
Write the number as a word,

84
00:04:53,299 --> 00:04:54,844
and the job never finishes.

85
00:04:55,744 --> 00:04:58,434
Name a good you don't have, and it never finishes.

86
00:05:00,234 --> 00:05:02,568
And here's the one that will catch you.

87
00:05:03,468 --> 00:05:06,639
You can't write, destroy three gleaners.

88
00:05:07,539 --> 00:05:09,525
The game takes the s off,

89
00:05:09,975 --> 00:05:12,902
looks for something called a gleaner, and finds nothing.

90
00:05:13,802 --> 00:05:15,677
So write enemies instead.

91
00:05:16,877 --> 00:05:19,733
At home, the farmers offer one job.

92
00:05:20,633 --> 00:05:22,006
I pay the levy,

93
00:05:22,456 --> 00:05:25,530
and now there are two, and the escort pays more.

94
00:05:27,330 --> 00:05:31,022
I take both, and here they are in the Quest Log.

95
00:05:31,922 --> 00:05:35,626
I engage the escort, and on arrival it's done.

96
00:05:37,426 --> 00:05:40,373
The miners' office has my two new jobs.

97
00:05:41,273 --> 00:05:44,105
I take them, and the clock on the relay run is running.

98
00:05:45,905 --> 00:05:47,963
The survey wants a dead ship,

99
00:05:48,413 --> 00:05:49,982
and I know where one is.

100
00:05:50,882 --> 00:05:53,955
And the patrol wants enemies,

101
00:05:54,405 --> 00:05:55,921
and I know where those are too.

102
00:05:57,121 --> 00:05:59,212
The Gleaners will deal with me now,

103
00:05:59,662 --> 00:06:01,351
so I take their salvage.

104
00:06:03,151 --> 00:06:05,367
When it's done, watch the farmers.

105
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:08,041
My standing with them just dropped,

106
00:06:08,491 --> 00:06:09,934
and I never spoke to them.

107
00:06:11,734 --> 00:06:15,302
Now the relay run takes me home, inside its ten minutes.

108
00:06:16,202 --> 00:06:17,586
And look at the farmers' list.

109
00:06:18,486 --> 00:06:21,798
Patrol is back, and it pays a little more than last time.

110
00:06:23,598 --> 00:06:26,328
That's the thing to remember about a job.

111
00:06:27,228 --> 00:06:28,202
It never runs out.

112
00:06:29,102 --> 00:06:33,536
So think about how often you want a crew to be able to please each side.

113
00:06:34,736 --> 00:06:35,738
Now it's your turn.

114
00:06:36,638 --> 00:06:40,404
Write one job for each side that only that side would offer.

115
00:06:41,304 --> 00:06:42,883
Make one of them tier two.

116
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:45,712
Make one that costs the crew somewhere else.

117
00:06:46,612 --> 00:06:49,246
And put one against the clock, and let it fail once.

118
00:06:51,046 --> 00:06:53,576
Next time, your universe gets a story,

119
00:06:54,026 --> 00:06:56,066
with a beginning and an end.
